{
  "$schema": "../_schema/enemyRoles.schema.json",
  "kind": "enemyRoles",
  "source": "claude",
  "notes": "Plan 7 Track N: the six enemy roles (combat design \u00a76) and their stats by CR, 0 to 30. A creature takes the last row at or below its CR (rows for CR 21\u201329 fall back to the even row below). Modelled on 5e's monster statistics by challenge rating, adjusted for linear combat: AC and to-hit follow the 5e scale (to-hit a point above it at CR 1/2\u20132, where published foes hit harder than the table). HP is a typical published monster's HP at the CR, scaled down for a party that makes one attack a turn: the whole of it up to CR 1/2, falling to 60% at CR 5, 45% at CR 12 and 40% from CR 20, so a fight at the intended level takes about as many rounds as in 5e. Damage is one blow a turn, 70% of 5e's damage per round (a fixed 2.5, 4, 5 and 7 at CR 0 to 1/2). Then by role, against that standard: brute \u00d71.35 HP, \u22121 AC, \u00d71.2 damage on d12s; skirmisher \u00d70.85 HP, +1 AC, +1 to hit, \u00d70.85 damage on d6s; archer \u00d70.7 HP, \u22121 AC, +1 to hit, \u00d70.8 damage on d8s (a volley hits everyone on a tile); caster \u00d70.6 HP, \u22122 AC, +1 to hit, \u00d70.7 damage on d6s against each member on the tile it blasts; swarm (one of many units) \u00d70.45 HP, \u22121 AC, \u00d70.6 damage on d4s; leader \u00d71.1 HP, +1 AC, +1 to hit, \u00d70.9 damage on d8s, and the rally (RALLY_BONUS). WIS (morale) is CR/4 plus brute and swarm \u22121, skirmisher 0, archer +1, caster and leader +2. Light blows use a smaller die. Role numbers not in the rows: an archer's and a caster's range is `reach`, a caster's blast is its `damage` on every member on the tile, a swarm's unit HP is its `hp`, the rally and the volley penalty are constants. Provisional: Track B's fight simulation tunes them. Our own numbers, written by Claude.",
